    <item>
        <title><![CDATA[What is FootfallCam?]]></title>
        <pubDate>2026-10-30 01:47:18</pubDate>
        <dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
        <description></description>
        <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>FootfallCam is a people-counting solution that measures how many visitors enter your store, how they move through it, and how long they stay. The sensors are installed at entrances and key zones, and the data flows into a central dashboard where you can view traffic by store, by day, or by hour. It turns visitor behaviour into numbers you can act on, rather than guesswork.</p>]]></content:encoded>
        <wp:post_id>20007</wp:post_id>
        <wp:post_date>2026-10-30 01:47:18</wp:post_date>
        <wp:post_date_gmt>2026-10-30 01:47:18</wp:post_date_gmt>
        <wp:comment_status>closed</wp:comment_status>
        <wp:ping_status>closed</wp:ping_status>
        <wp:post_name><![CDATA[faq-7]]></wp:post_name>
        <wp:status>publish</wp:status>
        <wp:post_parent>0</wp:post_parent>
        <wp:menu_order>7</wp:menu_order>
        <wp:post_type>ufaq</wp:post_type>
        <wp:is_sticky>0</wp:is_sticky>
        <category domain="ufaq-category" nicename="footfallcam"><![CDATA[FootfallCam]]></category>
    </item>
    <item>
        <title><![CDATA[Why do retailers need people counting when they already have sales data?]]></title>
        <pubDate>2026-10-30 01:47:18</pubDate>
        <dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
        <description></description>
        <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Sales data tells you what was bought, but not how many opportunities you missed. Knowing that 500 people entered and 50 purchased gives you a conversion rate, which is a far more useful measure of store performance than sales alone. It also lets you tell the difference between a slow day caused by low traffic and one caused by poor in-store execution.</p>]]></content:encoded>
        <wp:post_id>20008</wp:post_id>
        <wp:post_date>2026-10-30 01:47:18</wp:post_date>
        <wp:post_date_gmt>2026-10-30 01:47:18</wp:post_date_gmt>
        <wp:comment_status>closed</wp:comment_status>
        <wp:ping_status>closed</wp:ping_status>
        <wp:post_name><![CDATA[faq-8]]></wp:post_name>
        <wp:status>publish</wp:status>
        <wp:post_parent>0</wp:post_parent>
        <wp:menu_order>8</wp:menu_order>
        <wp:post_type>ufaq</wp:post_type>
        <wp:is_sticky>0</wp:is_sticky>
        <category domain="ufaq-category" nicename="footfallcam"><![CDATA[FootfallCam]]></category>
    </item>
    <item>
        <title><![CDATA[What metrics can we get from the system?]]></title>
        <pubDate>2026-10-30 01:47:18</pubDate>
        <dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
        <description></description>
        <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The core metrics are visitor count, conversion rate, dwell time, peak hours, and repeat visits. Depending on the configuration, you can also measure zone-level traffic, queue length, and staff-to-customer ratios.</p>]]></content:encoded>
        <wp:post_id>20009</wp:post_id>
        <wp:post_date>2026-10-30 01:47:18</wp:post_date>
        <wp:post_date_gmt>2026-10-30 01:47:18</wp:post_date_gmt>
